\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces Specifications per project. ``Median words'' is the median size of a specification. ``By agent'' is the share of specifications added by a commit attributed to an agent. ``Why'', ``AC'', and ``OOS'' are the shares of specifications with a section on what is built and why, with at least one acceptance criterion, and with a section on what is out of scope. ``Criteria'' counts acceptance criteria. ``Referenced'' is the share of specifications pointed to by at least one commit; ``With code'', the share added in the same commit as code; and ``Revised'', the share edited after their first implementing commit. ``Traced lines'' is the share of added lines that come from commits pointing to an existing specification.}}{12}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:specs}{{V}{12}{Specifications per project. ``Median words'' is the median size of a specification. ``By agent'' is the share of specifications added by a commit attributed to an agent. ``Why'', ``AC'', and ``OOS'' are the shares of specifications with a section on what is built and why, with at least one acceptance criterion, and with a section on what is out of scope. ``Criteria'' counts acceptance criteria. ``Referenced'' is the share of specifications pointed to by at least one commit; ``With code'', the share added in the same commit as code; and ``Revised'', the share edited after their first implementing commit. ``Traced lines'' is the share of added lines that come from commits pointing to an existing specification}{table.5}{}}
