\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {VI}{\ignorespaces Projects and their adherence to the methodology. ``Agents'' lists the tools declared in commit trailers and in the \texttt  {README.md}, and ``Stack'' the main language and frameworks. ``Specs'' shows dated files over all specification files. ``Spec first'' is the share of \texttt  {Spec:}-tagged commits whose specification was added in an earlier commit. ``Trailers'' is the share of commits with both \texttt  {Agent:} and \texttt  {Spec:}. ``Authors'' counts distinct human commit e-mails. ``SLOC'' uses the official \texttt  {cloc} command; projects that reached 100,000 lines are highlighted in green. Other cells that fail a requirement are marked in bold.}}{13}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:adherence}{{VI}{13}{Projects and their adherence to the methodology. ``Agents'' lists the tools declared in commit trailers and in the \texttt {README.md}, and ``Stack'' the main language and frameworks. ``Specs'' shows dated files over all specification files. ``Spec first'' is the share of \texttt {Spec:}-tagged commits whose specification was added in an earlier commit. ``Trailers'' is the share of commits with both \texttt {Agent:} and \texttt {Spec:}. ``Authors'' counts distinct human commit e-mails. ``SLOC'' uses the official \texttt {cloc} command; projects that reached 100,000 lines are highlighted in green. Other cells that fail a requirement are marked in bold}{table.6}{}}
